From: cubie-a5e-openwrt <noreply@github.com>
Subject: configs: radxa-cubie-a5e: DRAM at 936 MHz

As Armbian does for this board
(patch/u-boot/v2026.07-sunxi64/board_radxa-cubie-a5e/edit-radxa-cubie-a5e-defconfig.patch):
936 MHz instead of the A523 default of 1200 MHz gives the DRAM timings
more margin, so that one set (with the fallback of patch 420) fits more
board revisions and memory chips. Profiles in config/dram can set
another clock (patch 430).

---
diff --git a/configs/radxa-cubie-a5e_defconfig b/configs/radxa-cubie-a5e_defconfig
index 3dc3b6c..1492e3f 100644
--- a/configs/radxa-cubie-a5e_defconfig
+++ b/configs/radxa-cubie-a5e_defconfig
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@ CONFIG_ARM=y
 CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI=y
 CONFIG_DEFAULT_DEVICE_TREE="allwinner/sun55i-a527-cubie-a5e"
 CONFIG_SPL=y
+CONFIG_DRAM_CLK=936
 CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_DX_ODT=0x07070707
 CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_DX_DRI=0x0d0d0d0d
 CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_CA_DRI=0x0e0e
